{
  "scenario_id": "tied-wash-does-not-erase-scoop",
  "description": "The knife's scoop of satay (e1) and its wash (e2) have identical timestamps, as when both fall in the same camera window; later the knife touches the plate (e3). Under the strict tie default (OQ-17) a wash tied with a transfer is applied first, so the wash cannot erase the peanut that arrives with the scoop, and the plate must hold. The event IDs put the scoop first on purpose: breaking the tie by event_id alone would apply the wash last, clean the knife and could let the plate pass. Holds for any k in (0, 1]: with the wash first, nothing cleans the knife after e1, so it carries k * 0.95 * 0.98 > 0 peanut and the plate gets k * 0.9 times that, also > 0, at e3. The path e1 -> e3 runs forward in time with no wash after the scoop, so exact reachability flags peanut whatever k is.",
